# Get an exercise's progress. Start the API with Aspire first, then send "Create an account" once.
@host = http://localhost:5279

### Create an account → 201. The requests below use its access token.
# @name createAccount
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user-{{$guid}}@example.com",
  "password": "password",
  "timeZone": "Europe/Zagreb"
}

### The groups → 200. A new account's groups can take a moment to appear.
# @name groups
GET {{host}}/api/v1/groups
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Create an exercise → 201. The requests below read its progress.
# @name createExercise
POST {{host}}/api/v1/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bench press",
  "groupId": "{{groups.response.body.$[0].id}}",
  "alsoWorksGroupIds": []
}

### The last 3 months → 200. A new exercise has no sessions, so points is empty.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/exercises/{{createExercise.response.body.$.id}}/progress?range=3m
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Every session → 200. Over 60 sessions, each point is a month and byMonth is true.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/exercises/{{createExercise.response.body.$.id}}/progress?range=all
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### A range that isn't one → 400 validation.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/exercises/{{createExercise.response.body.$.id}}/progress?range=2w
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### An exercise that does not exist → 404 exercise.not_found.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/exercises/0198a000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000/progress
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Not signed in → 401 unauthorized.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/exercises/{{createExercise.response.body.$.id}}/progress
